// Truth sources for the storefront-tour eval set.
//
// One source per RAW table the storefront model reads, and nothing else: no
// measures, no joins, no renames, no labels, no doc tags. A golden must not be
// able to inherit the bug it is meant to catch, so nothing here is imported
// from storefront.malloy.
//
// A golden query that needs a join declares it inline, at the query, where a
// reader can see it -- rather than the source carrying a relationship the
// model also carries.
//
// `data/` is a COPY of the model's own `data/`, not a symlink: a relative link
// does not survive Publisher installing the package, which copies the directory
// into publisher_data/<env>/<pkg>/. So these bytes CAN drift from
// examples/storefront/data if the example data is regenerated. That is caught
// rather than silent -- verify_goldens.py re-derives every golden here before
// every arm and refuses the run when a value has moved -- but regenerate both
// together.

source: t_order_items is duckdb.table('data/order_items.parquet')
source: t_customers is duckdb.table('data/customers.parquet')
source: t_products is duckdb.table('data/products.parquet')
source: t_regions is duckdb.table('data/regions.csv')
